      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "FOR SALE BY PRIVATE TREATY\nNEWTOWN, MAYNOOTH, CO. KILDARE. W23 Y5E5.\n\nTo organize a viewing or to place a bid on this property go to www.teamlorraine.ie or scan the QR code on the photograph section of this brochure.\n\n\"A home of real presence, in the very heart of Maynooth.\"\nTeam Lorraine Mulligan, national and international award-winning agents with over 25 years` experience, are proud to present this magnificent five bedroom detached residence, with three ensuite bedrooms, set on a mature and private C. 0.4 acre site in the very heart of Maynooth.\n\nBehind high electronic gates, a sweeping tarmac driveway leads to the house, framed by high walls and mature hedging. You feel completely secluded, yet the shops, cafés and university of this lively town are just a short stroll away. Homes of this calibre, in a setting like this, very rarely come to the market.\n\nBuilt around 22 years ago, the house has a handsome red brick façade with granite surrounds and sills. It has been upgraded by its owners with a level of finish you will rarely find elsewhere.\n\nFirst impressions are unforgettable.The grand entrance hall is crowned by a stunning hand carved sweeping timber balustrade. The generous kitchen and dining room flows into a light filled sunroom, the natural heart of the home for family life and entertaining. A sitting room, a separate living room, a versatile playroom, home office or gym, a utility room and a bathroom complete the ground floor.\n\nUpstairs, a wide and elegant landing leads to the main bedroom suite, with its walk-in wardrobe and private ensuite.Two further bedrooms also have their own ensuites, and the fourth double bedroom overlooks the front garden. The luxurious family bathroom has a large jacuzzi bath and an oversized shower. A spacious attic provides excellent storage.\n\nOutside, the private south facing rear garden is bathed in sunshine throughout the day and has been designed for easy, low maintenance living. The large, detached garage has a loft with exciting potential as a studio or family flat, subject of course to the relevant planning permission.\n\nAccommodation briefly comprises: An entrance hall, kitchen/dining room, sunroom, sitting room, living room, playroom/home office/gym, utility room and bathroom on the ground floor. Upstairs: landing, four bedrooms with three ensuite bathrooms, a walk-in wardrobe in the master bedroom and a large sized family bathroom and attic storage.\n\nEverything On Your Doorstep\nMaynooth town, Maynooth University, schools, shops, cafés, restaurants and bars are all within walking distance.\n\nEffortlessly Connected\nThe train station and bus routes are a short walk away, with fast connections to Dublin, and the M4 gives quick access to the city and the west.\nA rare family home, in a location that is simply hard to beat.\n\nINTEREST IS SURE TO BE STRONG.\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "GROUND FLOOR ACCOMMODATION\nGrand Entrance Hallway: (L Shaped) \nLight fitting, alarm pad, intercom system, sweeping beautifully hand carved wooden balustrade, carpet on hallway, floor tiles in entrance hallway. \n\nKitchen/Dining Room:7.35m x 5.20m\nRecessed lights, curtains, solid light oak fitted kitchen with ample wall and floor units, tiled splash back area, granite work tops, crystal display cabinets, pottery display cabinet, wine rack, large breakfast bar area, integrated dishwasher, floor tiles, archway leading to the sunroom, double doors leading to the living room area. \n\nSunroom: 4.5m x 3.0m\nWooden ceiling, recessed lights, blinds, wooden floor, French double doors leading to the back garden.\n\nUtility Room: 2.90m x 2.70m\nBlinds, fitted wall and base units, area fully plumbed, hot press with an immersion, floor tiles, back door leading to the garden.\n\nLiving Room: 4.00m x 4.00m \nRecessed lights, features a large bay window, blind, marble open feature fireplace, wooden floors, double doors leading to the kitchen/dining area.\n\nSitting Room: 5.20m x 4.50m\nLight fitting, wall lights, feature open fireplace, blinds, curtains, wooden floor.\n\nDownstairs bedroom/Playroom/Home Office: 3.60m x 2.80m \nLight fitting, curtains, sliding patio door leading to the back garden, wooden floors.\n\nDownstairs bathroom:2.20m x 1.60m\nShaving light and socket, corner shelving, wooden wall cladding, floor tiles, W.C. WH.B., antique style claw bath, voile, heated towel rail.\n\n\nFIRST FLOOR ACCOMMODATION\nLanding:\nCarpeted staircase with oak handrail and white spindles, decorative wall panelling, tall window with Roman blind, storage closet, and wood effect flooring.\n\nMaster Bedroom 1:4.50m x 4.00m\nBlind, curtains, Sliderobes wardrobes, carpet. \n\nEnsuite:2.30m x 1.80m\nWith a window, W.C., W.H.B., corner shower with glass doors, wall and floor tiles.\n\nWalk in Wardrobe:2.30m x 2.10m\nHanging space and shelving space, carpet.\n\nBedroom 2: 4.40m x 3.30m\nBlind, curtains, Sliderobe wardrobes, wooden floor.\n\nEnsuite:2.90m x 1.00m\nW.C., W.H.B., shower with glass doors and an electric `Triton` shower, wall tiles and part floor tiles.\n\nBedroom 3: 4.00m x 3.15m\nFeatures a bay window, blind, curtains, fitted wardrobes, wooden floor. \n\nEnsuite:2.90m x 1.00m\nW.C., W.H.B., shower with glass doors, wall and floor tiles.\n\nBedroom 4:4.00m x 3.40m\nBlind, wooden floors, built-in wardrobes.\n\nBathroom2.90m x 2.40m\nFloor to ceiling wall and floor tiles, shaving light and socket, W.C., W.H.B., large corner jacuzzi bath, separate shower with glass shower doors. \n\n\nFEATURES INTERNAL\nThis is a superb family home with so much potential\nAll light fittings included in sale\nAll blinds included in sale\nAll curtains included in sale\nAll electrical white goods as described under kitchen section included in sale\nBeautiful, solid light oak fitted kitchen with lots of storage\nGranite work tops\nIsland unit\nHome has a large living room and sitting room\nHome comes with a sunroom\nSuperbly spacious\nHome comes with a downstairs bedroom/playroom/home office. \nAll bedroom`s upstairs are double bedrooms and three bedrooms have an ensuite each\nMaster bedroom also has a walk-in wardrobe\nBespoke wooden stunning balustrade\nSecurity alarm \nIntercom system\n\nFEATURES EXTERNAL\nPVC double glazed windows\nPVC facia & soffit\nGranite windowsills\nOutside garden lights\nLarge double detached garage\nElectric entrance gate\nSweeping tarmac driveway\nSolid block wall boundary\nMature gardens and trees\n\n\nOLD IS THE PROPERTY: Built in C. 2004\n\nWHAT IS THE FLOOR AREA OF THIS PROPERTY C.271.83sqm / 2925.95sqft\n\nBER RATING: B - 148.95kWh/m²/yr\n\nBER NUMBER: 119913374\n\nSERVICES: Mains water, mains sewerage, ESB, high speed broadband availability. \n\nHEATING SYSTEM: Gas heating.\n\n\nDISCLAIMER\nNotice to all parties viewing this brochure\n1. This brochure is provided for general guidance only. Nothing in it forms or constitutes an offer, contract, or binding agreement, and none of its contents should be treated as a statement of fact upon which any party can rely.\n2. Neither the Agent nor any member of staff has the authority to make representations or give warranties concerning this property on behalf of the vendor.\n3. Every description, measurement, and reference to condition, permitted use, or occupation has been prepared in good faith and is believed to be accurate at the time of preparation. However, prospective buyers and tenants are advised to verify all such details independently through their own inspection or enquiries rather than relying on this brochure alone.\n4. The Agent provides no warranty or covenant relating to the property. While familiar with its general appearance and layout, the Agent makes no claim to expertise regarding title or planning matters, and responsibility for confirming the sufficiency of such documentation rests entirely with the purchaser.\n5. Confirmation of service availability whether for current or intended use is the responsibility of the purchaser. The Agent offers no guarantees or representations on this matter.\n6. Boundaries, fences, hedges, walls, and ditches are not defined by either the vendor or the Agent, including any determination of party-structure status.\n7. Should any conflict arise between the information in this brochure and the formal contract of sale, the contract of sale will take precedence.\n8. References to \"Vendor\" and \"Purchaser\" throughout this brochure should be read as including \"Lessor\" and \"Lessee,\" or \"Landlord\" and \"Tenant,\" wherever the context applies.\n\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
